# Build-context excludes for the backend image (dev + prod Dockerfiles).
# The build context is ./backend, so paths here are relative to backend/.
#
# Goal: keep the image small and free of host-only / secret / regenerable
# files. Model artifacts the server loads at runtime are provisioned into a
# volume at deploy time (see DEPLOY.md), NOT baked into the image — so the big
# blobs under models/ and data/ are excluded here on purpose.

# Python caches / bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments (host-only)
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Secrets / local env — never bake into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests are not needed in the runtime image (prod installs runtime deps only)
tests/
test_*.py
*_test.py

# Project docs / scratch — not needed at runtime
*.md
COMPLETION_SUMMARY.txt
DELIVERABLES.md
FILES_CREATED.md
FILE_MANIFEST.md

# Large / runtime-provisioned model artifacts. These are mounted from a volume
# at deploy time (gallery_index.json, student.onnx) or are regenerable caches.
# Excluding them keeps the image lean and avoids stale copies shadowing the
# volume. The small committed bundles under models/ (lego_classifier,
# color_classifier) CAN ship in the image; if you prefer to volume-mount those
# too, add models/ here.
data/gallery_index.json
data/embeddings_cache.pkl
data/embeddings_cache.misses.txt
data/calibration_temperatures.json
*.mystery_backup
models/backup_*/
models/spark_*/

# Local dev compose / scripts that don't belong in the runtime image
docker-compose.yml
start_local.sh

# OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log
